The bug: Something calls HostProvider.get() before HostProvider.initialize() completes during extension activation. In VS Code extensions, activation is async.

The real fix pattern:
```typescript
// In host-provider.ts
let initPromise: Promise<void> | null = null;

export function initialize(): Promise<void> {
  if (!initPromise) {
    initPromise = doInitialize();
  }
  return initPromise;
}

export async function get(): Promise<HostProvider> {
  if (!initPromise) throw new Error('...');
  await initPromise; // wait for init to finish
  return instance;
}
```

This is a lazy-init singleton pattern. No mutexes. Just a promise gate.

